# NSEAP skill-spec.yaml — identity / level / route (MANDATORY for every new skill)

Copy this file to `references/skill-spec.yaml` when creating a NEW skill. Confirm defaults;
only change with reason. The level is decided by the NSEAP risk rules below.

```yaml
# Identity / level / route. Confirm defaults; only change with reason.
skill_spec:
  standard_id: nseap-skill-standard-v1
  skill_class: execution            # execution | meta_skill (if it makes skills)
  is_skill_of_skill: false          # true only for a Meta-Skill
  level: L5                         # Skill-L: L0..L5 (L5 = governed skill system)
  risk_route: Full                  # Lite | Full
  promotion_ceiling: staged         # HARD CAP — never higher than staged
  production_release_allowed: false # HARD LOCK — never true
  session_role: sub_skill           # sub_skill | master_task_skill
  owns_session: false               # true only for a Master Task Skill
  form: interpreted                 # interpreted | compiled
```

## Level decision (NSEAP §7.1 / §7.2)

Pick the level by risk, not by ambition:

| Condition | Level |
|---|---|
| Personal / low-risk / no sensitive data | L2 (or L3 if ontology-grounded) |
| To be shared / published / registered | **L5** |
| Handles customer / private data (resumes, sales, social, meetings, architecture) | **L5** |
| Has external actions (fetch scripts, network, write operations) | **L5** |
| Affects hiring / acceptance / business decisions | **L5** |
| Meta-skill (a skill that makes skills) | **L5 always** |

`risk_route`: `Lite` for reversible project-level reuse; `Full` for anything above.
`promotion_ceiling: staged` and `production_release_allowed: false` are ALWAYS the values —
never raise them.
